Written 2026-10-20. Nothing on this list is live yet. No cloud trigger has been changed and no `native_live` file has been created.

**How to switch one task (do them one at a time):**
1. Turn its cloud copy OFF in the Claude app (Scheduled list, the name in column 4). Proven call: `POST /v1/code/triggers/<trigger id>` with `{"enabled": false}`, then check that `GET` shows `enabled:false` (MAC_FIRST_PLAN §2.4).
2. `touch "Valley Pawn OS/fleet/state/native_live/<task>"`.
3. On the first run date, run the go-live check in the last column.

To go back: delete the `native_live` file and turn the cloud copy back on.

**Column 4 (cloud copy name):** this is the name the Claude app task list shows (the registry `displayName`; when a task has no display name, the app shows the task id). The titles were set when the copies moved to the cloud on 10/6–10/7. If a title in the app doesn't match, go by the trigger id.

